#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD1012A expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "AVISITN is declared while its primary AVISIT is not. AVISITN is one of the 20 catalogued secondaries (WildcardPairCatalogue), so the `*N` half seeds EXACTLY ONE expansion and `var_exists(\"AVISITN\") and not var_exists(\"AVISIT\")` is true. The column list is deliberately minimal: no other column ends in N or C (PARAMCD ends in D, AVAL in L), because every extra matching column silently adds an expansion and breaks the pinned count. Dataset granularity -> 1 violation. The pin is a bare row=1: the Output_Variable `*` expands to the PRIMARY name, which the rule fires on precisely because it is ABSENT, so it is omitted from the value map and any column pin would fall back to row 1's cell and assert something the finding does not say."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
col AVISITN type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | 40 | 1
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | ALB | 42 | 2
